# Bank 10 (runs at 0xA000). Directives: L label, C line comment, B block
# header, D data range, F row width.
#
# Mixed bank: 424 bytes of code and the rest data. It is mapped together with
# bank 9 (0x8000) for the fixed screens, and also together with bank 2
# (p00:4B0A) to load the scoreboard graphics.
D 0xA000 0xA0DB data_A000  219 bytes that no instruction points at with the address written in it: they sit right in front of the first compressed block of the bank. ASSUMPTION: they are the header or the first part of that same batch of graphics.
F 0xA000 16
D 0xA0DB 0xA3F4 graphics_patterns_2418  Compressed block that 0x4B17 passes to 0x4988 with HL=0x2418: it is dumped three times, once per third, adding 0x800. In this cartridge the patterns live at VRAM 0x2000 and the colours at 0x0000, the other way round from what the BIOS sets up.
F 0xA0DB 16
D 0xA3F4 0xA683 graphics_colours_0418  Compressed block that 0x4B20 passes to 0x4988 with HL=0x0418.
F 0xA3F4 16
D 0xA683 0xA758 graphics_sprites_1800  Compressed block that 0x4B29 dumps into VRAM 0x1800, which in this cartridge is the sprite pattern table.
F 0xA683 16
D 0xA758 0xA783 graphics_patterns_2780  Compressed block that 0x5C4B passes to 0x4988 with HL=0x2780.
F 0xA758 16
D 0xA783 0xA7A4 graphics_colours_0780  Compressed block that 0x5C54 passes to 0x4988 with HL=0x0780.
F 0xA783 16
D 0xA7A4 0xA809 graphics_sprites_1800_b  Compressed block that 0x5C5D dumps into VRAM 0x1800, the sprite pattern one.
F 0xA7A4 16
B 0xA809 A FOUR-SPRITES-PER-CRITTER ENGINE, ONLY FOR THE FIXED SCREEN
B 0xA809 This bank carries its own little engine, separate from the game's:
B 0xA809 eight slots of eight bytes at 0xE300, three spawners at 0xE500 and,
B 0xA809 for each slot, up to FOUR consecutive sprite entries in the buffer at
B 0xA809 0xEC80. Each critter comes into view one sprite at a time (byte 5
B 0xA809 counts how many it has) and moves with a pair of fixed displacements
B 0xA809 that its type gives it.
L 0xA809 set_up_screen   Clears the work RAM, sets up the three spawners and copies a routine for itself to 0xE710
C 0xA809 0x800 bytes from 0xE300 onwards, to zero
C 0xA816 The three spawners, from 0xA881 to 0xE500
C 0xA81C Three slots
C 0xA81F Four useful bytes of each one
C 0xA82E 0xE700, 0xE702 and 0xE704: where each one starts
C 0xA83D And 0x38 bytes of routine, copied to 0xE710 to run them from RAM
D 0xA849 0xA881 routine_for_RAM  56 bytes that 0xA840 copies with LDIR to 0xE710. They run from RAM, not from here.
F 0xA849 16
D 0xA881 0xA88D initial_values  Three groups of four bytes that 0xA816 spreads over 0xE500, leaving four empty bytes between one group and the next.
F 0xA881 4
L 0xA88D run_screen   A whole frame: moves the critters, lets the spawners release more, and builds the sprite entries
L 0xA897 move_the_eight   The eight eight-byte slots at 0xE300, one by one
C 0xA89B Eight slots
C 0xA89E An empty slot is left alone
C 0xA8A6 Eight bytes: the next slot
L 0xA8AE critter_step   While it is coming into view it keeps getting more sprites, and once whole it moves until it goes off screen
C 0xA8AE Byte 1: whether it has finished coming into view
C 0xA8B4 Byte 2: the frames until the next sprite
C 0xA8B8 Two frames per sprite
C 0xA8BC Byte 5: one more sprite
C 0xA8C2 Four sprites and it is whole
L 0xA8C9 critter_moves   The two displacements its type gives it; when it leaves through the bottom or the right, the slot is switched off
C 0xA8D0 The table at 0xA8F3: two bytes per type
C 0xA8D4 Byte 3, the row, plus its own
C 0xA8DC Past row 0xC0, out
C 0xA8E4 And byte 4, the column
C 0xA8EB Past column 0xF0, out too
D 0xA8F3 0xA90B displacements  Twenty-four bytes read by 0xA8D0.
F 0xA8F3 24
L 0xA90B run_spawners   The three spawners at 0xE500 release a critter every eight frames
C 0xA90F Three spawners
C 0xA912 Byte 2: the frames still to go
C 0xA917 Eight frames between one critter and the next
C 0xA91F Eight bytes: the next spawner
L 0xA927 release_critter   Picks the type from the table at 0xA989, looks for a free slot among the eight and fills it with its position, its drawing and its colour
C 0xA927 The spawner's type, times four
C 0xA92D Byte 5: which of the four is next
C 0xA932 Every four critters, 0x60 frames of rest
C 0xA93A One more for next time
C 0xA93E The table at 0xA989: four types per spawner
C 0xA946 The eight slots at 0xE300
C 0xA94C The first one with its first byte at zero
C 0xA956 The type, in the first byte
C 0xA958 No sprites yet, and two frames until the first one
C 0xA95E The type times three: the table at 0xA995
C 0xA96B The spawner's row plus its offset...
C 0xA970 ...and its column
C 0xA977 Byte 5 to one: one sprite already
C 0xA97D And its colour comes from 0xA9B9
D 0xA989 0xA995 table_A989  Twelve bytes read by 0xA93E.
F 0xA989 12
D 0xA995 0xA9B9 table_A995  Thirty-six bytes read by 0xA961.
F 0xA995 12
D 0xA9B9 0xA9C2 table_A9B9  Nine bytes read by 0xA97D.
F 0xA9B9 9
L 0xA9C2 build_sprite_entries   For each of the eight critters, four sprite entries in the buffer at 0xEC80
C 0xA9C2 Eight critters
C 0xA9C8 0xEC80: the sprite attribute buffer
C 0xA9CC Empty or full, each critter takes up its four entries
C 0xA9D8 Eight bytes: the next critter
L 0xA9E1 four_entries_off   0x10 bytes set to 0xE0: this critter's four sprites, off screen
L 0xA9E9 this_critter_entries   One entry per sprite in view, with the offset its type gets from the table at 0xAA46
C 0xA9E9 The type times eight: the table at 0xAA46
C 0xA9F7 Byte 5: how many sprites it has
C 0xA9FE The critter's row plus the offset...
C 0xAA02 ...and below 0xC0 it is not drawn
C 0xAA0B ...and its column
C 0xAA10 If the column wraps around, the sprite is switched off
C 0xAA26 Byte 6: the drawing
C 0xAA2B And byte 7: the colour
L 0xAA32 switch_off_leftovers   The sprites that have not come into view yet, with 0xE0 in all four bytes
C 0xAA32 Four minus the ones it has
C 0xAA39 0xE0: the VDP does not draw them
C 0xAA3B The four bytes of the entry
C 0xAA42 And on to the next one
D 0xAA46 0xAAA6 table_AA46  Ninety-six bytes read by 0xA9EF.
F 0xAA46 16
D 0xAAA6 0xAAB0 table_AAA6  Five words read by 0x831B in bank 2 with 0x47AE, indexing with (IX+6).
F 0xAAA6 w2
D 0xAAB0 0xAF29 data_AAB0  What the table above points to, and what 0x834F in bank 2 reads. 1145 bytes up to where the filler starts.
F 0xAAB0 16
D 0xAF29 0xC000 filler  0xFF filler up to the bank's 8192 bytes.
F 0xAF29 16
